window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f45de159970ea06a"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"devday-2026\">DevDay 2026</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-135e664cbdfe4444?anchor=devday-2026\">返回“最新动态”</a></p> <p>2026 年 9 月 29 日</p> <section> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">ChatGPT</h2> <h3 id=\"dot\">认识你的 dot</h3> <p>dot 是始终运行、能够持续承担任务的智能体。为你的 dot 设定目标，并定义它可以自主执行的操作。它可以在自己的计算机上跨已连接的应用工作，在对话之间持续推进任务，并把结果带回来供你检查。需要你作出判断时，它会主动联系你。dot 正逐步向符合条件的账户推出。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b\">了解 dot</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">可用性</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">管理员指南</a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">在不同设备间继续工作</h3> <p>在桌面端启动新的同步 ChatGPT Work 任务，然后在网页版或移动端继续。联网且已连接的计算机可以执行需要访问本地文件和工具的步骤。已有任务会继续使用创建时的原有模式。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669?anchor=continue-work-across-devices\">开始使用 Work</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">设置同步</a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt-space\">ChatGPT Space</h3> <p>将文件和 Pages 放在一起。使用 ChatGPT 起草和修改内容，直接编辑作品，并邀请协作者查看、评论或编辑。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8\">开始使用</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d\">Pages</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-2d083870d670ea3a\">与智能体协作</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">协作</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-315e17f0f4b919c1\">管理员指南</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"codex\">Codex</h2> <h3 id=\"codex-astra-ultrafast\">Codex 中的 Astra Ultrafast</h3> <p>在 Pro $500/月以及符合条件的 Enterprise 和 Edu 套餐中，可在 Codex 和 ChatGPT Work 使用 GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast。Enterprise 所有者可以控制访问权限；要求推理数据驻留在美国境外的工作区不符合条件。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Ultrafast 模式</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">套餐和用量</a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">可重复使用的云环境</h3> <p>描述你的开发环境，让 Codex 帮你准备并测试，然后发布该环境。新任务会在使用已准备文件系统的隔离工作区中启动。即使计算机处于睡眠状态，也可以从网页版、移动端或桌面端继续云端任务。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">云环境</a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-security-cloud\">Codex Security Cloud</h3> <p>使用 Security Cloud 插件扫描已连接的 GitHub 仓库，或监控新提交；该功能目前处于研究预览阶段。在创建草稿拉取请求（draft pull request）之前，可以先检查发现项、验证证据和补丁。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">设置 Security Cloud</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">威胁模型</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"sites\">Sites 和插件</h2> <h3 id=\"chatgpt_1\">使用 ChatGPT 登录</h3> <p>让用户使用 ChatGPT 登录；符合条件的 Plus 和 Pro 用户还可以在你的应用中使用 ChatGPT 套餐额度发起 AI 请求。商业登录目前仅面向选定合作伙伴开展有限试用。ChatGPT 套餐用量目前向开源合作伙伴和部分选定的私营客户提供。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/quickstart.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">快速入门</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">开源应用</a></p> <h3 id=\"site\">使用已连接数据构建 Site</h3> <p>构建一个 Site，让每位访客都能使用自己已连接的应用。启用后，插件可用于仅限工作区内部的 Site；访客可以选择自己的账户，并同意授权访问。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6?sectionMissing=load-visitor-data-via-plugins\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">使用插件加载访客数据（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6?sectionMissing=control-access-and-secrets\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">控制共享和访问权限（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">插件扩展</h3> <p>向 ChatGPT 添加侧边栏应用、对话面板、文件查看器和编辑器，以及表单。只有桌面应用支持在输入框中提及插件。Free 和 Go 套餐的网页版扩展即将推出。你可以把界面与插件的工具和技能打包在一起。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建扩展</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打包插件</a></p> <h3 id=\"mcp-events\">MCP Events</h3> <p>让用户请求 ChatGPT 监控 MCP 服务器的更新，并在收到符合条件的事件时执行操作。ChatGPT 要求使用 MCP 2.0，并支持根据 MCP Events 草案规范发送 Webhook。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-events.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建事件订阅</a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">网站批注</h3> <p>选择用户可以选中的内容、附加有用上下文，并添加控件，让用户在向 ChatGPT 发送反馈前预览修改。Browser Annotation API 可在受支持的桌面应用浏览器中使用。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-04a85e845544535d\">Annotations 扩展能力</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"api\">API</h2> <h3 id=\"gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</h3> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol 处理复杂编程和专业工作的表现接近 Astra，成本则更低。在提供该模型的地方，可通过 API 和 Codex 使用它。它在 Responses 中支持 Multi-agent beta，并支持 Standard、Flex 和 Batch 处理模式下的欧盟数据驻留。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API 模型</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">Codex 可用性</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/responses-multi-agent.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Multi-agent beta</a></p> <h3 id=\"api-astra-ultrafast\">API 中的 Astra Ultrafast</h3> <p>通过 Responses API 使用 GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast，缩短生成的输出词元（token）之间的间隔时间。可用性受速率限制约束，并采用全球处理和美国数据驻留。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/ultrafast-mode.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ultrafast 指南</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing?latest-pricing=ultrafast\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">价格（本地尚未收录）</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"enterprise\">Enterprise</h2> <h3 id=\"slack-teams-chatgpt\">在 Slack 和 Teams 中使用 ChatGPT</h3> <p>通过部署的已连接工具，将 ChatGPT 引入获准使用的对话。你可以配置谁能使用每个部署，以及每个部署可访问哪些频道。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Slack 和 Teams 指南</a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">团队任务</h3> <p>通过团队服务账户和已批准的连接，运行按计划或由事件触发的工作。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6\">设置团队任务</a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">工作区连接</h3> <p>为受支持的团队和工作流程连接由公司管理的账户。每个连接都使用相应已连接账户的权限。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">管理共享连接</a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">智能体安全</h3> <p>控制智能体可以使用哪些工具，以及它们如何访问文件和网络。为本地运行和 Codex Cloud 执行设置工作区策略；Work Cloud 有单独的控制项。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">Work 同步</a></p> </section>","en":"<h1 id=\"devday-2026\">DevDay 2026</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-135e664cbdfe4444?anchor=devday-2026\">Back to What's new</a></p> <p>September 29, 2026</p> <section> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">ChatGPT</h2> <h3 id=\"meet-your-dot\">Meet your dot</h3> <p>Dots are always-on agents that take on ongoing responsibility. Give your dot a goal and define what it can do on its own. It works across connected apps on its own computer, keeps making progress between conversations, and brings back results for your review. It reaches out when a decision needs your judgment. Dots are rolling out gradually to eligible accounts.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b\">Meet your dot</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">Availability</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">Admin guide</a></p> <h3 id=\"work-across-devices\">Work across devices</h3> <p>Start a new synced ChatGPT Work task on desktop and continue on web or mobile. An online, connected computer can run steps that need its local files and tools. Existing tasks keep their original mode.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669?anchor=continue-work-across-devices\">Get started with Work</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">Set up sync</a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt-space\">ChatGPT Space</h3> <p>Bring files and Pages together. Draft and revise with ChatGPT, edit your work directly, and invite collaborators to view, comment, or edit.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8\">Get started</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d\">Pages</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-2d083870d670ea3a\">Work with the agent</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">Collaboration</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-315e17f0f4b919c1\">Admin guide</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"codex\">Codex</h2> <h3 id=\"astra-ultrafast-in-codex\">Astra Ultrafast in Codex</h3> <p>Use GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast in Codex and ChatGPT Work on the Pro $500/month plan and eligible Enterprise and Edu plans. Enterprise owners control access; workspaces requiring inference residency outside the US aren't eligible.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Ultrafast mode</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">Plans and usage</a></p> <h3 id=\"reusable-cloud-environments\">Reusable cloud environments</h3> <p>Describe your development setup, let Codex prepare and test it, then publish the environment. New tasks start in isolated workspaces using the prepared filesystem. Continue cloud tasks from web, mobile, or desktop while your computer sleeps.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Cloud environments</a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-security-cloud\">Codex Security Cloud</h3> <p>Scan connected GitHub repositories or monitor new commits with the Security Cloud plugin, available in research preview. Review findings, validation evidence, and patches before creating a draft pull request.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Set up Security Cloud</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">Threat model</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"sites-plugins\">Sites &amp; plugins</h2> <h3 id=\"sign-in-with-chatgpt\">Sign in with ChatGPT</h3> <p>Let users sign in with ChatGPT and, for eligible Plus and Pro users, use their ChatGPT plan for AI requests in your app. Commercial sign-in is in a limited trial with selected partners. ChatGPT plan usage is available to open-source partners and selected private clients.</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/quickstart.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Quickstart</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open-source apps</a></p> <h3 id=\"sites-with-connected-data\">Sites with connected data</h3> <p>Build a Site that uses each visitor's own connected apps. Plugins in Sites are available for workspace-private Sites where enabled; visitors choose their accounts and consent to access.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6?sectionMissing=load-visitor-data-via-plugins\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Build with plugins (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6?sectionMissing=control-access-and-secrets\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Sharing and access (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Local page (section not recognized)</a></p> <h3 id=\"plugin-extensions\">Plugin Extensions</h3> <p>Add sidebar apps, conversation panels, file viewers and editors, and forms to ChatGPT. Composer mentions are available only in the desktop app. Free and Go web extensions are coming soon. Package the interface alongside your plugin's tools and skills.</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build extensions</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Package a plugin</a></p> <h3 id=\"mcp-events\">MCP Events</h3> <p>Let users ask ChatGPT to monitor updates from your MCP server and act when matching events arrive. ChatGPT requires MCP 2.0 and supports webhook delivery from the draft MCP Events specification.</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-events.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build event subscriptions</a></p> <h3 id=\"website-annotations\">Website annotations</h3> <p>Choose what people can select, attach useful context, and add controls to preview changes before sending feedback to ChatGPT. The Browser Annotation API works in supported desktop app browsers.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-04a85e845544535d\">Annotations Extensibility</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"api\">API</h2> <h3 id=\"gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</h3> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol offers near-Astra performance at a lower cost for complex coding and professional work. Use it in the API and Codex, where available. It supports Multi-agent beta in Responses and EU data residency with Standard, Flex, and Batch processing.</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API model</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">Codex availability</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/responses-multi-agent.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Multi-agent beta</a></p> <h3 id=\"astra-ultrafast-in-the-api\">Astra Ultrafast in the API</h3> <p>Reduce the time between generated output tokens with GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast in the Responses API. Availability is subject to rate limits, with global processing and US data residency.</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/ultrafast-mode.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ultrafast guide</a> <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing?latest-pricing=ultrafast\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pricing (not in this local snapshot)</a></p> </section> <section> <h2 id=\"enterprise\">Enterprise</h2> <h3 id=\"chatgpt-in-slack-and-teams\">ChatGPT in Slack and Teams</h3> <p>Bring ChatGPT into approved conversations with your deployment's connected tools. Configure who can use each deployment and which channels it can access.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Slack and Teams guide</a></p> <h3 id=\"team-tasks\">Team Tasks</h3> <p>Run scheduled or event-triggered work through a team's service account and approved connections.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6\">Set up Team Tasks</a></p> <h3 id=\"workspace-connections\">Workspace connections</h3> <p>Connect company-managed accounts for supported teams and workflows. Each connection uses the connected account's permissions.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">Manage shared connections</a></p> <h3 id=\"agent-security\">Agent Security</h3> <p>Control which tools agents can use and how they access files and the network. Set workspace policies for local and Codex Cloud execution; Work Cloud has separate controls.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">Work sync</a></p> </section>"};
